  "rule": "Return a live strategy to paper when any of: (a) its signal hit rate falls to or below 50% over a trailing 40-selection window; (b) its exchangeability p-value on the trailing window exceeds 0.50, i.e. the forecast has stopped disaggregating from noise; (c) its staking drawdown exceeds 10 flat units while the signal score is below the 50% break-even line; (d) it loses price agreement - the mean absolute difference between its fair line and the market exceeds 6 points for two consecutive windows, which means it has stopped being a forecast and started being an opinion.",
  "rationale": "Each clause targets a different failure. (a) and (b) catch a decaying model. (c) catches the exact case the split exists for, a losing signal kept alive by a hot staking run. (d) catches divergence from the market, which is a data or specification break rather than bad luck.",
